[E0505] Error: an owned `dyn` cannot hold a view
    ╭─[ err/704_an_owned_dyn_of_what_cannot_be_one/main.wip:21:48 ]
    │
 21 │ fn boxed<T: Shape>(value: T): own<dyn Shape> = own value
    │                                                ────┬────
    │                                                    ╰────── `T` may hold a view, in an instance that makes it one
    │
    │ Help: own what the view reads, or lend it as a `&dyn` for the call that needs it
    │
    │ Note: an owned `dyn` is kept where the type it was made of is no longer known, so nothing would say what a view inside it borrows, or keep that alive
────╯
